# ~/.config/zozobox/env on the box's Pi: the pi-ops env_file (deploy/pi.toml).
# Mode 600, owned by the service user, OUTSIDE the clone (~/apps). systemd
# reads it (EnvironmentFile=) when it starts app-zozobox.service; after an
# edit run: sudo systemctl restart app-zozobox
# deploy/host-setup.sh copies this template only when the file does not exist
# yet. Never commit the filled-in file.
#
# Format (systemd EnvironmentFile, pi-ops README "Secrets"):
#   - one KEY=VALUE per line; lines starting with # or ; are comments
#   - no `export`, and no spaces around =
#   - a value with spaces, #, \ or a double quote goes in single quotes
#     (KEY='a b#c'); nothing is escaped inside single quotes
#   - a value containing a single quote uses double quotes, with \" and \\
#   - $ is not expanded
#
# Until a value is filled in, the supervisor skips what needs it and says so
# in `journalctl -u app-zozobox`: no AI keys = no content or mood jobs; no
# cloud URL/token = no sync. The engine and the dashboard always run.

# Anthropic Console: a separate key for the button box, in its own workspace
# with a spend limit (SPEC 7.0).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=replace-me
# OpenAI: a key in a separate project with a budget (SPEC 7.0).
OPENAI_API_KEY=replace-me

# Cloudflare worker (cloud/worker/README.md): its PUBLIC_BASE_URL (an https://
# URL), and the same value as the worker's BOX_TOKEN secret. Sync is not
# started (and the token never sent) while either is a placeholder or the URL
# is not https.
ZOZOBOX_CLOUD_URL=replace-me
ZOZOBOX_BOX_TOKEN=replace-me

# Optional, non-secret overrides (see zozobox/content/pipeline.py):
# ZOZOBOX_CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# ZOZOBOX_TTS_VOICE=
# Supervisor (zozobox/run.py): RLIMIT_DATA in MB for each nightly, bootstrap
# and mood job (0 = no limit; size it from MemoryPeak, docs/DEPLOY.md step 1).
# ZOZOBOX_JOB_MEMORY_MB=384
